\tocItem notes \markup "Notes"

\markup {
  \left-column {
    \fill-line { \bold { Notes } }
    \wordwrap {
      Attempt to render source\footnote\super"1" "1. Paris: Sieber, n.d.https://imslp.org/wiki/Special:ImagefromIndex/651669/hfjn"
      using the Lilypond notation system.
    }
    \wordwrap {
      The source scan I worked from was incomplete : it was missing the last page of Player 2's part; that is, everything after M. 94
      of the first movement and all of the 2nd movement. I used Gérad Billaudot's edition\footnote\super"2"
      \wordwrap {2. Devienne, F. \italic { Six dous concertants pour deux bassons} , cahier 2. Revision de Maurice Allard, Gérard Billaudot, Editeur. 1975.}
      to complete the second player's part. I ignored all of the elements that may have been added by the editor, but then had
      to try to guess what articulations, dynamics, and ornatments where in the original source. I did this mostly by using the first player's
      part as a guide, since that part came from the original score. 
    }
  }
}
\markup {
  \center-column {
    \line { "VI Duetto" }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "First Movement" }
      \wordwrap {
	\bold { M. 108. } Followed same passage found in M. 46: removed grace notes (perhaps
	added by Billadout) and added staccatisimo articulation.
      }
      \vspace #1
      \fill-line {"Second Movement" }
      \wordwrap {
	Dynamic marks appearing in Billadout are removed throughout, since there are
	no dynamics given by source in Player One's part. Same with portato articulations.
	Removed slur markings and added slurs where indicate using Player One's part. The
	two parts aren't that similar, but I'd rather omit indications that may not
	have appeared in the orginal score that add indications that do not exist in the original.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold { MM. 1-2 } Used articulations from first two measures of Player One's part rather
	than the ones from Billadout. Used these articulations again on similar figures throughout.
      }
    }
  }
}